Fixture C (M6 spec 15): one ARC with deliberately NONTRIVIAL angles.
999
Centre (10,-5), radius 12, start 30 deg, end 200 deg, millimetres.
999

999
Every value is chosen so a mistake shows up:
999
 - 30 and 200 are not 0/90/180, so cos and sin are distinct irrational values
999
   and swapping start with end moves the endpoints somewhere obviously wrong;
999
 - the sweep 30->200 is 170 deg, so it is neither a half turn nor a quarter;
999
 - the centre is off the origin and has a NEGATIVE y, so dropping the centre or
999
   flipping the y axis is visible;
999
 - DXF stores these as DEGREES. If they reached the model unconverted, the
999
   start direction would be 30 RADIANS, which is 30 - 4*2pi = 1.867 rad = 107
999
   deg -- a different point entirely, which the geometric test measures.
